<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vsevolod the Big Nest</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1154">1154</a>–<a href="/years/1212">1212</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Vsevolod III</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vsevolod III, called the Big Nest for his many sons, was grand prince of Vladimir-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suzdal">Suzdal</a> from 1176 to 1212. He made Vladimir the strongest principality of north-eastern Rus' and dominated Novgorod and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryazan">Ryazan</a>. His sons divided his lands into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanages</a> such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rostov">Rostov</a> and Starodub, and his descendants included the later princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vsevolod-the-big-nest.jpg" alt="Vsevolod the Big Nest" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vsevolod_III_the_Big_Nest,_titular_1673.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
